<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>Best-Effort Structuring</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Schemes & Rules</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">Best-Effort Structuring</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block"><strong>Best-Effort Structuring</strong> is the primary transitional rule for pre-cutover content processed after 15 November 2026: institutions SHALL extract <code>&lt;TwnNm&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;Ctry&gt;</code> from the original unstructured address where reliably derivable and place residual content in up to two <code>&lt;AdrLine&gt;</code> elements. The CUTOVER2026 keyword is the exception of last resort where extraction fails.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How Best-Effort Structuring works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>The rule applies to R-transactions and warehoused payments during the Period 4 stabilisation window (cutover plus a maximum of three months). After the CUTOVER2026 keyword is withdrawn, long-tail R-transactions must be handled with Best-Effort Structuring alone (§40.2).</p></div> <p class="src">Source: PMPG Hybrid Postal Address v1.12 §7 / §38 (§3.3-A, p42–43); §40.2; the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 PART XIII, Appendix I Q3.</p> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-mandate">ISO 20022 deadline — the structured address mandate</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
